<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> (Joke) SCP</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Comedy, Weird</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Standard SCP, extensive addenda describing discoveries.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Finally, an answer to where all those Lost Christmas specials come from, where the end up, and why they're all so awful. This <em>extensive</em> research demonstrates both the anomalous nature of their appearance, and offers an occult explanation for their poor quality and untimely release.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Although the '78 Star Wars special is probably the best known, some paranormal entity has been producing anomalous media since at least 1976. The addenda include selected summaries such as &quot;The 007 Days of Christmas&quot; (1976), &quot;A Very Rocky Christmas&quot; (1979), &quot;The Blues Brothers: A Mission From God&quot; (1998), and &quot;The Festivus Reunion&quot; (2015), all featuring appropriately aged (or decayed) actors reprising their original roles.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Let's be honest. The universe would be a better place if we could blame every holiday special on some unknowable force.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> G. D! B B, A GG C B B A A G.</p>

